- How is the school doing?
	Hope: How is the school doing?
	Zanele: The children are reading. Forty of them are reading, and two years ago that number was eleven.
	Zanele: What I do not have is anywhere to put forty children.
	Zanele: We are in a hall that holds thirty comfortably, on a tin roof that makes rain into an event, and I teach two groups because they will not fit at once.
	Zanele: But they are reading. I want to say the reading part first, because it is the more important of the two facts.
